        "notes": "Penn State gives no watering style ('no overwatering or underwatering'), UMD calls the light level medium. Penn State's temperature figure is day 65-75 F. No fetched page states toxicity, so it stays unknown, never safe. Interval: RHS 'water once the top few centimetres of compost start to dry out' (finger test or lifting the pot), 'less water in winter'; NC State says only 'moist, well-drained mix', susceptible to rot if overwatered (no rule). One source with a rule, so 7 stays unconfirmed. Pot and season: 13 cm pot, bright indirect light, room temperature, growing season. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives days, left as before (from_knowledge_verify). Watering style let_top_dry from RHS (water once the top few centimetres of compost start to dry out)."
